From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:46:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(goals): no turn budget by default, pause only when stuck

A /goal was capped at 20 turns and then paused whatever the progress. It now
has no turn cap by default (goals.max_turns 0; 0 and None stay 0 instead of
falling back to 20) and runs until the judge says done, the user pauses or
clears it, or it is stuck. goals.stuck_turns (default 3, 0 = off) pauses a goal
whose judge reason repeats that many turns in a row, or whose no-tool turn
repeats the previous reply, with a plain reason and /goal resume to continue.
A positive goals.max_turns still caps. Status shows 'turn N', the set
confirmation drops the budget, and the /goal help says so. Kanban goal-mode
workers keep their own cap.
